## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates practical, production-ready handling of partial data quality failures in a Delta Live Tables pipeline, balancing correctness with availability.

## Key Concepts
- Staging vs downstream separation
- Expectations-based quality checks
- Quarantine and audit of invalid data
- Late data handling with watermarking
- Deduplication strategies across micro-batches

## Code Example
```javascript
import dlt
import pyspark.sql.functions as F

@dlt.table
def raw_events():
  return spark.read.format("cloudFiles").option("cloudFiles.format","json").load("/mnt/events/raw")

@dlt.table
def valid_events():
  df = dlt.read("raw_events")
  return df.filter(F.col("event_time").isNotNull() & F.col("user_id").isNotNull())

@dlt.table
def invalid_events():
  raw = dlt.read("raw_events")
  valid_ids = dlt.read("valid_events").select("event_id").distinct()
  return raw.join(valid_ids, "event_id", "left_anti")

@dlt.table
def clean_events():
  return dlt.read("valid_events")
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor and alert if invalid_events growth spikes?
- What changes would you make to support reprocessing of invalid data after fixes?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical ability to design a DLT-based ingestion, including schema drift handling, per-tenant partitioning, and end-to-end quality checks in a beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- Delta Live Tables (DLT)
- Data quality with expectations
- Schema drift tolerance
- Rollback/version control
- Lineage and monitoring

## Code Example
```python
import dlt

@dlt.table
def bronze_logs():
  return spark.read.parquet("s3://bucket/logs/")

@dlt.table
def silver_logs(bronze_logs):
  df = bronze_logs.filter("event_id IS NOT NULL")
  return df.select("tenant_id", "date", "event_id", "event_type", "payload")

@dlt.table
def gold_metrics(silver_logs):
  return silver_logs.groupBy("tenant_id").agg(count("event_id").alias("events"))
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to handle schema changes without breaking downstream dashboards?
- How would you monitor and alert on data quality failures in production?
